%I A399704 #22 Sep 21 2026 12:24:37
%S A399704 3,6,5,9,7,8,9,11,11,14,13,14,15,20,17,22,19,20,21,24,23,24,25,26,27,
%T A399704 30,29,33,31,32,33,34,35,37,37,38,39,45,41,49,43,44,45,48,47,48,49,50,
%U A399704 51,54,53,54,55,56,57,62,59,63,61,62,63,64,65,69,67,68,69
%N A399704 a(n) is the smallest integer >= n such that (n-1)*n/2 + a(n) divides (n-1)! * a(n).
%C A399704 a(n) is well-defined and <= (n-1)*n/2, as this number satisfies the divisibility condition.
%C A399704 a(n) = n iff n*(n+1)/2 | n! iff n+1 | 2*(n-1)!.
%C A399704 If n+1 is composite, then for any nontrivial divisor f of n+1 we have n-1 = n+1-2 = f*(n+1)/f-2 >= 2*f-2 >= f, hence f | (n-1)!, so n+1 | (n-1)! | 2*(n-1)!, so a(n) = n.
%C A399704 If n+1 is prime, then Wilson's Theorem says n! == -1 (mod n+1), so (n-1)! == 1 (mod n+1), so n+1 does not divide (n-1)!, and as n+1 is odd, n+1 does not divide 2*(n-1)!, so a(n) > n.
%C A399704 For k >= n, (n-1)*n/2 + k | (n-1)! * k = (n-1)! * ((n-1)*n/2 + k - (n-1)*n/2) iff (n-1)*n/2 + k | (n-1)! * (n-1)*n/2. Hence a(n) = d - (n-1)*n/2 where d is the smallest divisor of (n-1)! * n*(n-1)/2 with d >= n + (n-1)*n/2 = n*(n+1)/2. If n >= 4 and n+1 is prime, then n is even, so n+2 | (n-1)! | (n-1)! * (n-1), so d := n*(n+2)/2 is a solution, so a(n) <= n*(n+2)/2 - (n-1)*n/2 = 3*n/2.
%C A399704 Together: a(n) = n for composite n+1, and n < a(n) <= 3*n/2 for prime n+1.
%C A399704 Conjecture: The tuple (1,...,n-1,a(n)) minimizes s(v) as well as p(v) and p(v)/s(v) for v being an n-tuple of distinct positive integers with s(v) | p(v), where s(v) and p(v) denote the sum and the product of the entries of v.
%H A399704 Markus Sigg, <a href="/A399704/b399704.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 3..10000</a>
%e A399704 a(3) = 3 because 1+2+3 = 6 divides 1*2*3 = 6. a(10) = 11 because 1+...+10 = 55 does not divide 10! = 3628800, but 1+...+9+11 = 56 divides 9!*11 = 3991680.
%o A399704 (PARI) a399704(n) = {
%o A399704   my(p = (n-1)!, s = (n-1)*n/2);
%o A399704   for(i = n, oo, if((p*i) % (s+i) == 0, return(i)))
%o A399704 };
%Y A399704 Cf. A000142, A000217, A057568, A063520, A065015, A104173, A399852.
%K A399704 nonn,easy,new
%O A399704 3,1
